 ## Tier 2: Close Collaboration

 This is a review process to approve CMS-developed software to be released open source at [github.cms.gov](https://github.cms.gov/). If you would like your repository to be released, please complete the following steps.
+
+### Evidence provenance and phase ownership
+
+Record the checklist, template and metadata-schema revisions reviewed, the review
+date, candidate commit or digest, and responsible actor. Distinguish inspected
+evidence from reported approvals; a retained checklist copy does not certify current
+policy or transfer another project's waiver.
+
+Keep file/section presence, substantive content, JSON parsing, schema compliance,
+factual accuracy, source vulnerability analysis, secret scanning and qualified
+human review as separate results. One identified scan can support several items
+when its exact scope and outcome are referenced, without counting it as independent
+checks. A linter pass does not establish institutional approval.
+
+Separate repository setup, local preparation, authorized upload, post-upload
+administration and hosted evidence. The responsible authority records the actual
+bootstrap sequence for the selected risk route, including which controls precede
+or follow upload. Do not require an unuploaded workflow's successful run. For
+Indelegible, the recorded sequence is completed sole human review/OSPO approval,
+human fast-forward push, then human-admin controls and exact-candidate hosted
+observation, followed by subsequent enforcement. An actual server rejection stops
+publication; no bypass or protection disablement is authorized. Protect the actual
+approved branches; examples do not require dev, releases, websites or packages.
+
+Before publication, scan proposed current content and then, after the final commit,
+all required available non-shallow committed history. Record scanner version,
+configuration, refs, candidate and result. Reconcile hosted version/scope and extra
+merge refs before claiming parity. Preserve original findings and use narrowly
+authorized treatment, never an unrecorded broad suppression or payload repetition.
+
+Retain specifically required files. Give shared prose one canonical owner and link
+exact sections from those files. Clearly label optional automation and DCO; do not
+convert examples into prerequisites or infer a required-file waiver.
+

